# <coordinator-settings-home>/environment-registry  (NOT committed -- per-machine)
#
# Spec backlink: docs/plans/2026-09-07-compose-the-environment-story-and-select.md
# (chunk C3). Read by `_environment_story.resolve_environment_story` via
# `coordinator/hooks/scripts/_environment_selection.py::default_registry_path`.
#
# THIS FILE IS AN EXAMPLE, NOT A LIVE REGISTRY. It ships in the repo so an
# operator has a format to copy; it is never read by the resolver from this
# path and carries no real environment ids. Do not add a real box's
# environment id here and commit it -- this template's job ends the moment
# you copy it.
#
# WHAT AN OPERATOR SETS: one line per environment id this box (or a fleet
# of boxes sharing one image) might report, naming which composed story
# that id resolves to. An id with no line here resolves to `strictest` --
# see `_environment_story.py`'s six failure modes, of which "unknown
# environment id" is one; that is not an error state, it is the safe
# default for anything not explicitly named.
#
# WHERE THE REAL ONE LIVES: copy this file to
#   ${COORDINATOR_SETTINGS_HOME:-${CLAUDE_HOME:-$HOME}/.coordinator-claude-settings}/environment-registry
# (the exact path `_environment_selection.default_registry_path()` resolves
# to). It is gitignored there, like every other machine-local settings-home
# artifact -- this is per-machine or per-image configuration, never a
# tracked value shared across the fleet.
#
# FORMAT: flat `<environment_id>: <story_name>` lines, one per environment
# id. `#` starts a comment (whole-line only); blank lines are ignored. The
# first matching line for a given id wins if an id is duplicated -- see
# `_environment_story._read_registry_entry`'s own docstring for why that is
# deliberate rather than an accident to fix. `<story_name>` must be a name
# admitted via `_environment_story.register_story` (currently `strictest`,
# admitted unconditionally, and `ephemeral-cloud-vm`, composed in
# `_environment_stories.py`) -- naming anything else resolves to
# `STRICTEST_STORY` exactly like an absent line would, per failure mode 5
# ("unknown environment id") in `_environment_story.py`'s module docstring.
#
# Example entries -- an ephemeral cloud VM image bakes its own id in at
# provisioning time (matching whatever `default_sentinel_path()` reads on
# that image) and this registry maps that id to the composed story:

# my-cloud-vm-image-2026-09: ephemeral-cloud-vm

# A workstation box needs no line at all: an id with no entry here (or no
# sentinel file to produce an id in the first place) resolves to
# `strictest`, and that is a positive claim this plan makes deliberately --
# see docs/plans/2026-09-07-compose-the-environment-story-and-select.md
# § "The composed set, and the argument for each member" for why there is
# no `workstation` story to name here.
